What nethack needs is some REALLY NASTY low-level monsters.  I only
find the game fun to play in the first 10 levels of the dungeon, when
it takes real ingenuity and scraping the barrel to keep yourself alive.

But after that, things get a little too easy.  If you get Mjollnir,
dragons die in 3 hits ... what kind of a dragon is THAT?  Even the
Minotaur is a wuss, at least by the time you meet him.

I am not necessarily suggesting monsters with many many hit dice ...
although something like a Godzilla (500 hitpoints, stomps and crushes
and bites for 3d50 damages, but slow) would be fun.  I think monsters
need new special abilities.  A couple of suggestions:

- Touch of polymorph.  A monster with this would randomly polymorph
   one item in your pack if it succeeded.  To prevent someone from
  shedding all their valuables and going up to it to get their junk
  polymorphed, this monster should also have a hit-to-damage.

- Touch of slowing.  Player's speed is cut by 1/2 for a while.  Unicorn
  horns don't help.

- Gaze of fear (a la Moria) - Makes player unable to attack anything for
  a few turns.

- A strong, superfast (2x speed) monster

- Monsters that summon other monsters, besides demons and the Wiz

Basically, if we are going to have things like boots of speed and Mjollnir
in this game, though I like them, I would like there to be some monsters
that a character with -20 armor class, boots of speed, and Mjollnir would
be afraid of and have to attack very cautiously.

I think it is a great temptation to baby the player too much so that people
won't face the trauma of losing a 12th level player they've worked on for
hours, but I think keeping the player safe is a great mistake.

Numakils are great - the shock of losing yr player in 3 hits to something
you thought was a rothe is the kind of thing that keeps you awake.

Another, rather bizarre notion - if monster stats & abilities are kept
in a uniform database, why not have the game INVENT new monsters, a
few different ones every time you start up.
"The red newt-dragon breathes fire!
You hit the red newt-dragon! -- more ---
You destroyed the red newt-dragon!"

hmm ... ?

This talk of new and different levels is fine, but we need more DANGER!
(ps those of you who keep getting killed on the 4th level may think that
that's a sick joke, but seriously, the game does need more difficulty
beyond the 10th level or so.)

